<title>Australia: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to April 25.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>Rank Name			  Price     pct change</p>
<p>1   Southern Pac Petroleum   3.53	    229.91</p>
<p>2   Oilsearch		    3.01	    140.80</p>
<p>3   Nat Aust Bank	     17.07	     50.26</p>
<p>4   Howard Smith		10.85	     48.63</p>
<p>5   CSL			    7.05	     46.88</p>
<p>6   Leighton		     5.82	     44.78</p>
<p>7   James Hardie		 3.90	     44.44</p>
<p>8   Fletcher Energy	    3.68	     39.39</p>
<p>9   Transurban		 885.00	     38.93</p>
<p>10  Australian Gas Light     7.44	     38.55</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>Rank Name			  Price     pct change</p>
<p>1   Goldfields		   2.03	     -37.92</p>
<p>2   Acacia			 1.94	     -37.82</p>
<p>3   Plutonic		     5.00	     -33.77</p>
<p>4   Sons of Gwalia	     5.75	     -33.14</p>
<p>5   Newcrest Mining	    4.01	     -32.94</p>
<p>6   RGC			    4.65	     -31.01</p>
<p>7   Great Central Mines	2.75	     -28.94</p>
<p>8   Davids			 1.34	     -27.96</p>
<p>9   Normandy		     1.63	     -26.91</p>
<p>10  News Corp prefs	    4.94	     -23.53</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
